!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
! SEQUENCES section (used to build up the full line in various variations) !!!!!
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
! Remember that MAD-X "SEQUENCE" as default takes the reference point
! to be the centre of the element.






! -- CA.LINAC ----------------------------------------------------------------
! from RFgun to CA.BTV0390 included.
!
! Based on: Survey file for the CALIFES line in CTF3 - CLEX
!
! F. Tecker
! 25 Jan 2008
!
! Based on an initial MAD-X sequence generated by Michel Fontaine
!
! Verified with the plan 71 E022 DM- 0080 000 RG
! that shows the whole CALIFES line (provided by N.Chritin)
!
! The bending magnet placement is designed such that the
! following elements do not move their position if the length
! of the bend is changed in the file.
! The placement in a MAD-X sequence uses the path length for
! the positioning.
! As I have given the crossing point of the tangents for the
! spectrometer line (at 21.2454m from the cathode), the position
! in the sequence has to be corrected by the straight length
! that is in the bend (L/[2cos(a/2)]),
! i.e. 1/2 the arc length s = L*a/2/sin(a/2)
!
! The same offset has to be applied for the elements following
! the bend with relative placement.
!
! The positioning was verified for the coordinates of CAS.BTV0420
! (for almost 0 and real length of the bend)
!
! Modified 25.03.2008 (FT):
!    Quad length changed to 0.220 m (as in linac and TBTS files)
! Modified 20.04.2017 (DG):
!    The elements are defined above and I finish with last BTV.
!    An additional spectro line is defined for that: CA.CADUMP
! Modified 30.06.2022 (KNS):
!    3xx quadrupoles were moved in 2019 to make room for new EOS
! Modified 13/1/2023 (KNS)
!    Taking measurements by Wilfrid & co
!    of everything after accelerator exit into account
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

! L_CALIFES   = 14.9539+L_ACS_LIL_mech/2 + 1.220+0.440*2+0.470+0.295+0.165+0.240 + L_CALIFES_FUDGE;  what is L_CALIFES_FUDGE ???
!L_CLEAR_LINAC   = 14.9539+L_ACS_LIL_mech/2 + 1.220+0.440*2+0.470+0.295+0.165+0.240 ;
                                                                                !Measurement 17/2/2023
                                                                                ! Length of Califes, from the cathode to previous position of BTV0390
                                                                                ! BTV0390 has since been moved
L_CLEAR_LINAC   = 21.00 ;   ! New end for the LINAC sequance to include also the ICT0395

S_QFD0350_M = L_CLEAR_LINAC-(0.4036+1.220+2*0.440+L_Q_mech/2);                             !Measurement 12/1/2023
                                                                                ! Middle of QFD350 quadrupole,
                                                                                ! originally taken as ref. for measurements in the machine.

CA.LINAC : SEQUENCE, L=L_CLEAR_LINAC;
! Acceleration part:
CA.CANON.1.S,  AT= 0 ;
CA.CANON.1.E,  AT= 0.00001 ;
CA.DHG0130,  AT=  0.317  ;
!CA.ICT0210,  AT=  1.4996 ;  ICT is located at 1.64 m from cathode not at 1.5
!CA.LAS0215,  AT=  1.500  ; ! From mechanical drawing!  40 um difference??
CA.LAS0205,  AT=  1.4996 ;  ! It is neiher ICT nor screen. It is the laser port. perhaps necassary to keep in MADX due to aperture restriction on beam AA Jan 2024
CA.ICT0210,  AT=  1.64   ; ! Measurement by Wilfrid using ruler. not pricise
